{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Joan Baez feels like a natural next choice because Melanie, Jonathan Edwards, and Simon & Garfunkel reflect my interest in folk songs and distinctive voices.",
    "Eagles strongly fits my classic rock listening and preference for greatest-hits collections; Hall & Oates also connects with the melodic pop-rock appeal of The Cars.",
    "Elvis fits the familiar oldies listening reflected in AM Gold: The Mid-'60s and my other hits compilations."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Perry Como does not connect as strongly with the folk and classic rock songs I want today, even though it is another best-of collection.",
    "A Day Without Rain feels less suited to my current desire for familiar hits than the folk and rock collections.",
    "I cannot tell enough from the title Kiss to feel confident that it matches what I want to hear."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A greatest-hits label helps, but it does not make every artist equally appealing to me.",
    "My interest in older music does not mean I want every older vocal style; folk and classic rock are stronger draws today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection among Melanie, Jonathan Edwards, and Simon & Garfunkel matters especially strongly, which makes Joan Baez a more compelling choice than many other compilations.",
    "Enjoying pop albums does not mean I would choose every pop hits collection now; ABBA and Cher appeal, but Eagles and Joan Baez take priority.",
    "My recent Christmas album reflects an occasion and does not replace the broader folk and classic rock interests in my history."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in familiar hits, but my strongest choices depend on the particular folk and classic rock sound, not just the compilation format."
}"}
